---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Docs — TPM">
  <section style="padding: 3rem 0 2rem;">
    <h1>Docs</h1>

    <h2>Quick start</h2>
    <pre><code>npm install -g tpm

cd your-product-repo        # TPM reads the codebase from the CURRENT DIRECTORY
tpm init                    # creates .tpm/ in this repo
tpm audit https://your-product.com   # URL = deployed site TPM walks</code></pre>
    <p style="max-width: 44rem; color: #4d4d4d;">
      TPM runs <strong>from inside your repo</strong>. The codebase (cwd) feeds Stage A's Lean
      Canvas reconstruction; the URL argument is the deployed product TPM walks with Playwright
      for Stage B. Omit the URL entirely to run code-only (Stage A only, no browser walk).
    </p>
    <p style="max-width: 44rem; color: #4d4d4d;">
      First audit runs on our hosted Cloudflare Workers AI (one per device).
      For unlimited audits, <a href="/self-host">self-host on your own Cloudflare</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>The six-stage method</h2>
    <p>TPM runs a deterministic pipeline. Each stage checkpoints to disk and can be replayed independently. Artifacts live in <code>.tpm/artifacts/&lbrace;audit_id&rbrace;/</code>:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>lean-canvas.yaml</code> — Stage A: what the builder intended</li>
      <li><code>paths.yaml</code> — Stage B: what actually happens per persona</li>
      <li><code>delta.yaml</code> — Stage C: the structured difference</li>
      <li><code>problems.yaml</code> — Stage D: ranked by leverage argument</li>
      <li><code>solutions.yaml</code> + <code>prototypes/*.html</code> — Stage E: top-5 fixes</li>
      <li><code>spec.md</code> + <code>spec.pdf</code> — Stage F: the PM deliverable</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Commands</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>tpm init</code> — initialize <code>.tpm/</code> in the current project</li>
      <li><code>tpm audit [target]</code> — run a full audit</li>
      <li><code>tpm audit --gateway byo</code> — force BYO mode for this run</li>
      <li><code>tpm report [audit_id]</code> — show a prior spec.md</li>
      <li><code>tpm config get/set/show</code> — inspect or change config</li>
      <li><code>tpm self-host</code> — print the BYO setup guide</li>
      <li><code>tpm cost</code> — show Neuron spend per audit / per stage / per model</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Privacy &amp; security</h2>
    <p style="max-width: 44rem;">
      TPM runs on your machine. In <strong>hosted-trial mode</strong>, prompts flow through
      our Cloudflare Worker proxy at tpm-api.sina-b35.workers.dev — logged server-side as token counts only
      (not content), unless you opt into debug mode. In <strong>BYO mode</strong>, prompts go
      directly from your CLI to your own Cloudflare account; nothing touches our infrastructure.
    </p>
    <p style="max-width: 44rem;">Source code never leaves your machine in either mode.</p>

    <h2>More</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/sinameraji/tpm">Source on GitHub</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/sinameraji/tpm/blob/main/docs/the-method.md">The method</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/sinameraji/tpm/blob/main/docs/architecture.md">Architecture</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/sinameraji/tpm/blob/main/docs/patterns-authoring.md">Authoring patterns</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
